drm/panel: Sharp LS041Y3 (Nokia N800/N810), chained after the S1D13745

The LS041Y3 takes pixels from the Epson S1D13745; the host drives its
MIPI DBI command interface on McSPI1 CS1 (9-bit words, 4 MHz). After
Nokia's lcd_mipid.c:
- detection by display ID (0x83 LS041Y3, 0x45 Philips LPH8923), and
  whether the bootloader left it on (status: sleep out, display on);
- enable: sleep out, init string (0xc2, then 24 data lines), display on;
  disable: display off, sleep in; 120 ms between sleep in and out;
- the LS041Y3 ESD check every 5 s while on: the self-diagnosis bit that
  sleep out flips, and from revision 0x88 a register read through the
  test commands; on failure sleep in and out again;
- backlight through drm_panel_of_backlight (the Tahvo backlight).

s1d1374x now attaches the next bridge on its port 1 (the panel, through
the panel bridge) and no longer provides a fixed mode; the mode is the
panel's, with the omapfb DISPC timings. DT: the panel on mcspi1 with
nreset on gpio30 (NOLO's LCD tag), graph S1D13745 port 1 -> panel.

